source_unit_ids":["u1","u10","u14","u15","u29"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"definitions","explanation":"Gift is not exhaustively defined. Additional returns and incentives may qualify, rather than necessarily qualifying. Product types expressly include certain fund types and funds from certain fund houses. Whether a benefit is a genuine fee discount and whether it has the required promotional connection require judgment.","source_unit_ids":["u8","u13","u14"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"exceptions","explanation":"The fee-or-charge discount parenthesis qualifies gifts under the selected restriction, including gifts linked to a product type. It does not exempt conduct from other provisions. No actual-distraction test or structured-product exemption is stated for this control. The text does not settle which fees qualify or the treatment of mixed benefits.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u13","u14","u15"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"modality","explanation":"The selected wording is 'should not', reinforced by 'requirement' and 'will be bound'. It supports a normative restriction, without establishing that every breach is a statutory offence. 'May be considered a gift' leaves classification contingent. The formalized outcome identifies an offer caught by this restriction, not liability or overall compliance.","source_unit_ids":["u10","u13","u14","u24"],"status":"PROPOSED"},{"dimension":"time","explanation":"The restriction concerns offering gifts in promotion, without a supplied commencement date, deadline or transitional rule. The FAQ date, 2010-09-30, identifies a referenced document and is not established as the control's effective date. Later advertising guidance does not supply that date.","source_unit_ids":["u14","u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"},{"dimension":"dependencies","explanation":"Paragraph 3.11 and FAQ question 1 are material unprovided authorities. The packet's external-authorities.23ec46 dependency has no source hash. Statutory, Handbook and advertising provisions remain separate contextual dependencies; their full content or current versions cannot be inferred from the extracts.","source_unit_ids":["u7","u10","u12","u14","u28","u29","u30","u31"],"status":"AMBIGUOUS"}],"questions":["Does the selected restatement apply to all investment-product promotions by the defined distributors, or only their SFC-authorised-fund promotions?","What do the applicable version of paragraph 3.11 and the referenced FAQ answer say about actor scope, gifts, product linkage and qualifying discounts?","Which fees or charges can be discounted, and how should a package combining a discount and a separate benefit be divided for assessment?","What commencement date and source versions apply to the conduct under review?"],"readings":[{"assumptions":["Each evaluation concerns one identified benefit offer to one client; a campaign requires assessment of every relevant offer.","The actor must be a distributor as defined in u1; the Code's title alone does not expand this actor definition.","The general investment-product wording in u14 determines product scope.","Product-type linkage in the promotion is sufficient; proof of actual distraction is not an additional condition.","Unknown classification or scope facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"Intermediaries who distribute these funds (distributors)","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"If gifts are offered in such a way that they are linked to a particular type of investment product, such as certain types of funds or funds offered by certain fund houses, then such gifts will be bound by this requirement","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"as they may be considered a gift that should not be offered to investors.","unit_id":"u13"}],"distinction":"A defined distributor's non-discount gift promoting a specific investment product outside SFC-authorised funds can be caught. The strongest uncertainty is whether the circular's fund-specific setting limits the otherwise general product wording.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the distributor description in u1.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit is offered to a client; actual acceptance or delivery is unnecessary for this offer fact.","name":"benefit_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift, assessed before applying the express discount exception; an additional return or incentive is not automatically classified as a gift.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within u14's exception; merely including a discount elsewhere in a package is insufficient to establish this fact.","name":"benefit_is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The offer is made in promoting a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to the client, including promotional linkage to a type such as funds from certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The product or product type to which this benefit's promotion is connected falls within the circular's SFC-authorised-fund subject matter.","name":"promotion_concerns_authorised_funds","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor benefit_offered_to_client has_product_promotion_connection)"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["Does paragraph 3.11 confirm the general product scope of this restatement despite the circular's fund-specific subject?"],"statement":"Selected control: general-product gift-offer restriction. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, an identified benefit offered to a client in promoting a specific investment product or a particular product type is caught by the 'should not offer' restriction if it is a gift and is not a qualifying fee-or-charge discount. This includes promotional linkage to a fund type or fund house. The restriction does not depend on the arrangement being a structured product or on demonstrated distraction.","subject":"Whether an identified offer is caught by the selected paragraph-10 gift restriction"},{"assumptions":["Each evaluation concerns one identified benefit offer to one client; a campaign requires assessment of every relevant offer.","The actor must be a distributor as defined in u1; the Code's title alone does not expand this actor definition.","The circular's SFC-authorised-fund context limits this selected application of the general wording quoted in u14.","Product-type linkage in the promotion is sufficient; proof of actual distraction is not an additional condition.","Unknown classification or scope facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"This circular summarises the Securities and Futures Commission’s (SFC) recent observations of licensed corporations’ practices in offering and promoting SFC-authorised funds.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"in offering such returns or other incentives in promoting SFC-authorised funds","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"when offering or promoting funds, distributors should not offer additional returns","unit_id":"u15"}],"distinction":"The same distributor's gift promoting only a different investment product is outside this selected application, while gifts connected to SFC-authorised funds remain covered. Outside scope does not mean permitted under the full Code. The strongest uncertainty is that u14 itself states no express SFC-authorised-fund limitation.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the distributor description in u1.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit is offered to a client; actual acceptance or delivery is unnecessary for this offer fact.","name":"benefit_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift, assessed before applying the express discount exception; an additional return or incentive is not automatically classified as a gift.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within u14's exception; merely including a discount elsewhere in a package is insufficient to establish this fact.","name":"benefit_is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The offer is made in promoting a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to the client, including promotional linkage to a type such as funds from certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The product or product type to which this benefit's promotion is connected falls within the circular's SFC-authorised-fund subject matter.","name":"promotion_concerns_authorised_funds","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor benefit_offered_to_client has_product_promotion_connection promotion_concerns_authorised_funds)"},"local_id":"reading_2","questions":["Is the fund-specific context a limit on this circular's selected application, or merely the occasion for restating a broader control?"],"statement":"Selected control: fund-context gift-offer restriction. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, an identified benefit offered to a client in promoting a specific SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of such funds is caught by the 'should not offer' restriction if it is a gift and is not a qualifying fee-or-charge discount. Product-type linkage includes relevant funds offered by certain fund houses. Structured-product status and actual distraction are not additional conditions.","subject":"Whether an identified offer is caught by the selected paragraph-10 gift restriction"}]},"normative":{"coverage":[{"reason":"Defines distributors and the circular’s fund-distribution context.","status":"INTERPRETED","unit_id":"u1"},{"reason":"Background heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u2"},{"reason":"Observed additional features; does not itself classify every feature as a gift.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u3"},{"reason":"Standing-instruction services provide surrounding context.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u4"},{"reason":"Describes marketing practices without limiting the selected control to public campaigns.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u5"},{"reason":"Guaranteed-returns heading.","status":"CONTEXT","unit_id":"u6"},{"reason":"Identifies the separate statutory regime.","status":"CONTEXT","